    {
      "memory_id": "m002",
      "summary": "The Anniston Historical Society runs a weekly Saturday series of leadership workshops for young women in a small-group mentoring setting, focused on leadership activities and community service projects to encourage community leadership. The program includes a \"Timeline of Me\" activity, oral history indexing of recordings from women who marched and organized in the sixties, and a \"Quilt of Voices\" sewing session in the fourth session led by someone with over fifty years of quilting experience; participants may be complete beginners, so options include fabric glue and markers or hand-stitching with embroidery circle helpers. A final showcase may feature older ladies from a church choir singing old spirituals.",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-28T20:41:11+08:00",
      "topics": [
